      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 Elsevier Ireland Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "Many studies have revealed a role of YKL-40 as a new inflammatory biomarker in angiogenesis, inflammation, atherosclerosis and cardiovascular events. Thus, the aim of this study was to investigate the association of serum YKL-40 level with coronary collateral development and SYNTAX score in patients with stable coronary artery disease."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "A total of 165 patients who had ≥90% stenosis in at least one major coronary artery were prospectively enrolled in the study. Collateral degree was graded according to Rentrop-Cohen classification. Patients with grade 2 or 3 collateral degree were included in good collateral group and patients with grade 0 or 1 collateral degree were included in poor collateral group. The patients were also classified according to SYNTAX criteria, those with low (≤22) and those with high (>22) SYNTAX score."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Serum YKL-40 and hs-CRP levels were significantly lower in good collateral group. Furthermore, YKL-40 level showed significant positive correlations with SYNTAX score (r=0.486, p<0.001) and hs-CRP level (r=0.340, p<0.001). In multivariate regression analysis, serum YKL-40 (odds ratio: 0.928; 95% confidence interval: 0.917-0.940; p<0.001), duration of ischemic symptom and total occlusion were independent predictors of good collateral development. In ROC curve analysis, a YKL-40 value cut-off point of ≥168.5 predicted the high SYNTAX score with a sensitivity of 81.0% and specificity of 72.4%."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "Increased serum YKL-40 level was related with poor collateral development and high SYNTAX score. According to these findings YKL-40 can be used as a predictor of good collateral development and high SYNTAX score."
          }
        ]
      },
